  isp_base: "1d4x10 plus M.E. attribute number, +2d6 per level of experience"
  powers: ["Empathy", "Object Read (Psychometry)", "See Aura", "Telepathy", "Mind Block"]
natural_abilities:
  - name: "Natural Psionics"
    description: "Every noro is born with psionic ability and is considered a MAJOR psionic. The five powers above are innate and cost no selection; the noro psychic and noro mystic warrior O.C.C.s develop them much further."
  - name: "Average Life Span"
    description: "250 years."
  - name: "Size"
    description: "Seven to eight feet tall (2.1 to 2.4 m), 180 to 240 pounds (82 to 109 kg)."
  - name: "Appearance"
    description: "Thin, spindly humanoids with oversized black eyes, long slender fingers, six fingers on each hand and six toes on each foot, and narrow mouth and lower jaw. Instead of hair the head grows bony spikes of varying length; some noro wear them as a mohawk-like crest and others shave them off."
extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified against a 200 dpi render of
    printed 62, which carries the whole stat block. The render and the cache
    agree line for line.
  - "M.D.C.: By armor or psionics only" - the noro is an S.D.C. being, so there
    is no mdc_base. S.D.C. itself is given as "Standard", with no formula, so it
    falls through to the core rule via CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS; hit points are the
    stated P.E. plus 1D6 per level.
  - HORROR FACTOR: NONE, stated outright rather than omitted.
  - Object Read and Possess Others are the book''s spellings. The catalog holds
    them as "Object Read (Psychometry)" and "Mentally Possess Others"; the
    catalog names are used, since a second row would manufacture a duplicate.
  - THE O.C.C. RESTRICTION IS NOT EXPRESSIBLE AND IS NOT WRITTEN. The book says
    a noro may take any O.C.C. "excluding those that require heavy cybernetics
    or bionic conversions". `occ_restrictions` matches an O.C.C.''s `occ_group`,
    and the five legal groups are clergy, men-of-arms, optional, magic and
    psychic - none of which is "requires cybernetics". Writing a restriction
    that matches nothing would fail OPEN and offer everything anyway, which is
    what it does now, so the rule is recorded here and in the Lore instead of
    being faked.
  - A RACE CARRIES NO xp_table. The book gives the noro no ladder of its own -
    printed 183 heads that column "Noro Psychic / Promethean (First Stage)",
    which is the O.C.C.''s ladder, not the race''s - and `frontmatter.md` is
    explicit that a race carrying one wins over the occupation''s and silently
    drops it.
  - The book''s Psionic Powers line says the five are what ALL noro have, so they
    are granted by name rather than picked; there is no `powers_starting` and no
    `categories_allowed`, because a plain noro selects nothing.
