## Lore

The noro are an ancient and advanced race: thin, spindly humanoids seven to
eight feet tall, with oversized black eyes, six fingers to a hand and bony
spikes where hair would be. They are not as numerous as humans or wolfen and
they are an influential force in the Consortium anyway, because they got there
first and because they are all psychics.

They came from Noro-Gor in the Corkscrew Galaxy, and their innate psionics drove
their technology as much as their science did - a race that can watch telekinesis
work understands physics early. They went from the Stone Age to spaceflight in
five thousand years.

## Ironee

The thing that made the noro what they are is the worst thing they ever did. One
orbit out from Noro-Gor lived the ironees, an older race that had developed more
slowly and sat at roughly early-twentieth-century Earth. Facing overpopulation,
a noro nation-state called Zorak built ships and went to take the planet, and
other noro nations followed with their own expeditions and their own alliances.

What the noro did not know was that several ironee nations were on the verge of
atomic theory. The war drove them to build the weapon, and then to use it on
each other as much as on the invaders - and neither side understood what
radiation would do. Within a few years Ironee held almost nothing alive. The
ironees had expelled the invaders and destroyed themselves doing it.

Psionic societies are bad at keeping secrets, and the extermination of a
sentient race brought down every noro government under the rally cry *Never
Again*. Every noro citizen now makes a pilgrimage to shrines built in the ruins,
where the psychic agonies of the war are still vivid three thousand years on.

## The conscience of the CCW

The noro fate, as the psychics who first visited those ruins reported it, is to
be communicators, diplomats and peace-bringers. They founded a planetary
government that promised never to conquer, colonised only uninhabited worlds,
and learned that total pacifism was impossible only when a Kittani fleet came
for Noro-Gor - after which they resurrected their martial technology on the
understanding that it was for defence.

Sixty per cent of all TVIA inspectors are noro. Many are active against
would-be conquerors and tyrants beyond CCW reach, and their Mystic Warriors turn
up assisting the Transgalactic Empire''s Freedom Fighters or working alongside
cosmo-knights, phase adepts and undead slayers.

A small percentage have forsaken the ways of peace, and those become notorious
rogues and outlaws.

## GM Notes

A noro may take any O.C.C. except those needing heavy cybernetics or bionic
conversion - the app cannot enforce that, so it is a table rule. Spacers, CAF
soldiers and the psionic O.C.C.s (mind melter, noro psychic, noro mystic
warrior) are the common adventuring choices.

The noro work closely with humans. They find the wolfen and the seljuk
unsettling in their aggressiveness, and explain it away by saying neither race
has felt the guilt of genocide first-hand.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'noro');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'noro';

